#!/bin/sh
# Every header under inst/include compiles alone, with no other header
# before it, under -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Werror, as C11 and as C++17,
# both standalone (ZT_STANDALONE, no R) and against R's headers. And the
# header's version is the package's (design-kernel section 8, R10.4).
# Run from the package root: sh tools/check-headers
set -eu
cc=${CC:-cc}
cxx=${CXX:-c++}
tmp=$(mktemp -d)
trap 'rm -rf "$tmp"' EXIT
rinc=$(R CMD config --cppflags 2>/dev/null || true)
# zufast's headers, which the key model includes (LinkingTo: zufast).
zinc="-I$(Rscript -e 'cat(system.file("include", package = "zufast"))')"
fail=0
for h in $(cd inst/include && find . -name '*.h' | sed 's|^\./||' | sort); do
  printf '#include <%s>\nint zt_header_check_tu;\n' "$h" > "$tmp/tu.c"
  cp "$tmp/tu.c" "$tmp/tu.cpp"
  for mode in standalone r; do
    if [ "$mode" = standalone ]; then def="-DZT_STANDALONE"; inc="$zinc"; else def=""; inc="$rinc $zinc"; fi
    $cc -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Werror $def -Iinst/include $inc \
      -fsyntax-only "$tmp/tu.c" || { echo "FAIL: $h as C11 ($mode)"; fail=1; }
    $cxx -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Werror $def -Iinst/include $inc \
      -fsyntax-only "$tmp/tu.cpp" || { echo "FAIL: $h as C++17 ($mode)"; fail=1; }
  done
  echo "ok: $h"
done
want=$(sed -n 's/^Version: *//p' DESCRIPTION)
got=$(sed -n 's/^#define ZUTABLE_VERSION "\(.*\)"$/\1/p' inst/include/zutable/version.h)
if [ "$want" != "$got" ]; then
  echo "FAIL: zutable/version.h says $got, DESCRIPTION $want"
  fail=1
fi
exit $fail
